<mjml lang="en">
  <mj-head>
    <!--
      PROBE — Outlook background-image void (2026-08-12).
      Not a catalog page. Send dist/probe_outlook-background-image_live.html
      through EN to EoA and read outlook2021_win11_* and m365_w11_* first.

      THE FINDING THIS TESTS
      Every background-image section in the v4 catalog renders as a flat
      colour slab in the Word engine, while MT's NGS reference renders its
      photo. Verified 2026-08-12 against the delivered HTML of both:

        * not delivery  — our v:rect / v:fill / background= / url() all
                          arrive with absolute URLs
        * not the image — all four hero photos are baseline JPEG (SOF0)
        * not the block — the "Hello World" band fails too, so there is no
                          working counter-example in our own catalog

      The one markup difference: our section sets background-color AND
      background-url; NGS sets only background-url. That makes MJML emit
      bgcolor="…" on the Outlook conditional table and color="…" on the
      v:fill. NGS emits neither, and the slab we see is exactly that colour
      — so the fallback appears to be beating the image in Word.

      VARIANTS (identical content, only the fallback plumbing differs)

        A CONTROL   background-color + background-url, exactly as shipped.
                    Expected: flat maroon slab, no photo.
        B NGS SHAPE background-url only. Expected: the photo renders.
                    Cost if adopted bare: an image-blocked Outlook shows
                    white, with no brand fallback at all.
        C WRAPPER   background-url only on the section, the fallback colour
                    moved OUT to an mj-wrapper behind it. Expected: the
                    photo renders AND a blocked image still falls back to
                    brand colour, because the wrapper paints behind the
                    section rather than inside its VML rect.

      VERDICT RULE
      Prefer C if it shows the photo — it is the only variant that keeps a
      fallback. Fall back to B if C also slabs (which would mean the
      wrapper's own bgcolor reaches the rect). If A renders the photo too,
      the diagnosis is wrong and nothing should be changed on this evidence.

      Check every other client as well: whichever variant wins must not
      regress Apple Mail / iOS / Gmail, where A already renders correctly.
    -->
    <mj-breakpoint width="600px" />
    <mj-title>PROBE — Outlook background image</mj-title>

    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text
        color="#000000"
        font-size="18px"
        font-weight="400"
        font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif"
        line-height="24px"
        css-class="wysiwyg"
      />
      <mj-image padding="0" />
    </mj-attributes>

    <mj-raw>
      <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no" />
    </mj-raw>
    <mj-include path="./styles.css" type="css" />
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body css-class="email-body" background-color="#ffffff">

    <!-- START: Probe Label A -->
    <mj-section css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">A — CONTROL (COLOR + URL)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Probe Label A -->

    <!-- START: Probe A Control -->
    <mj-section
      css-class="image-block block"
      background-color="#362229"
      background-url="assets/photo-river.jpg"
      background-size="cover"
      background-repeat="no-repeat"
      background-position="center center" padding="16px 0 16px"
    >
      <mj-group>
        <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        <mj-column width="550px" vertical-align="middle">
          <mj-text color="#ffffff" align="center" padding="0 32px 8px">A — expect a FLAT SLAB in Outlook</mj-text>
        </mj-column>
        <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
      </mj-group>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Probe A Control -->

    <!-- START: Probe Label B -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">B — URL ONLY (NGS SHAPE)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Probe Label B -->

    <!-- START: Probe B Url Only -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude
      css-class="image-block block"
      background-url="assets/photo-river.jpg"
      background-size="cover"
      background-repeat="no-repeat"
      background-position="center center" padding="16px 0 16px"
    >
      <mj-group>
        <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        <mj-column width="550px" vertical-align="middle">
          <mj-text color="#ffffff" align="center" padding="0 32px 8px">B — expect the PHOTO in Outlook</mj-text>
        </mj-column>
        <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
      </mj-group>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Probe B Url Only -->

    <!-- START: Probe Label C -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">C — FALLBACK ON A WRAPPER</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Probe Label C -->

    <!-- START: Probe C Wrapper Fallback -->
    <mj-wrapper background-color="#362229" padding="0">
      <mj-section
        css-class="image-block block"
        background-url="assets/photo-river.jpg"
        background-size="cover"
        background-repeat="no-repeat"
        background-position="center center" padding="16px 0 16px"
      >
        <mj-group>
          <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column width="550px" vertical-align="middle">
            <mj-text color="#ffffff" align="center" padding="0 32px 8px">C — expect the PHOTO, with a brand fallback behind it</mj-text>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        </mj-group>
      </mj-section>
    </mj-wrapper>
    <!-- END: Probe C Wrapper Fallback -->

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
